-- title:
--   Negation preserves extendability of Picard points to a place
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N_0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, and a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{P} : \mathtt{DRModelPackageLevel}\ N_0\ p$, whose structural morphism `toBase N₀ p` over $\operatorname{Spec}(R_p)$ is assumed proper. Let $D$ be a relative $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ designation for `toBase N₀ p`, that is a scheme $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(R_p)$ together with a zero section, and let $hD$ witness that $D$ represents the functor of line bundles rigidified along the cusp section $\mathfrak{P}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ whose fibres over algebraically closed points are algebraically equivalent to zero. The further data fix the generic fibre picture and are grouped as follows: a corresponding representability datum $hDQ$ for the base change of $D$ to $\mathbb{Q}$ together with an isomorphism $hPQ$ between its Poincaré bundle and the base change of that of $hD$; an Abel–Jacobi morphism $ajQ$ from the curve over $\mathbb{Q}$ to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\ \mathbb{Q}).\mathrm{toBase}$ sending the cusp section to the zero section and pulling the Poincaré bundle back, at every point $x$ of every field-valued fibre, to $\mathcal{O}(x)\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\varepsilon_{\inf}}$; a comparison morphism $kQ$ between the fibres over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and over $\mathbb{Q}$; the induced morphism $ajbar$ on $\mathfrak{P}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ with its cusp point $\bar\varepsilon$; and a bijection $\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldBar}(N_0p)$ onto the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D$, assumed additive for the relative group law attached to $hD$, Galois-equivariant, and compatible with $ajbar$ in the sense that the class of $[x]-[s]$ goes to $x \circ ajbar$ whenever $s$ is the cusp point. Finally let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The conclusion is that for every $x \in J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, if $\mathrm{pts}(x)$ extends to the place $A$, i.e. factors through an $A$-point of $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho$, then so does $\mathrm{pts}(-x)$.
--
--   The statement is one half of the assertion that the points of $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ extending to a given place $A$ above $p$ form a subgroup of the $A$-points of the relative Picard scheme of the Deligne–Rapoport model; the companion result treats sums. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.extendsToPlace_pts_smul_sub`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.extendsToPlace_pts_smul_sub), which reduces extendability statements for differences of Hecke or inertia translates to generators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel_extendsToPlace_pts_neg.lean

